{"name":"Aspiration","hex":"#a08a80","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"aspiration","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The act of aspiring or ardently desiring; an ardent wish or desire, chiefly after what is elevated or spiritual (with common adjunct adpositions being to and of)."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The action of aspirating.","A burst of air that follows the release of some consonants."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/aspiration"}],"entries":[{"title":"Aspirated consonant","blocks":[{"text":"In phonetics, aspiration is a strong burst of breath that accompanies either the release or, in the case of preaspiration, the closure of some obstruents. In English, aspirated consonants are allophones in complementary distribution with their unaspirated counterparts, but in some other languages, notably most North American languages, South Asian languages and East Asian languages, the difference is contrastive."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/44/IPA_Unicode_0x02B0.svg/330px-IPA_Unicode_0x02B0.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aspirated_consonant","wikidata":"Q320433"},{"title":"Voiceless glottal fricative","blocks":[{"text":"A voiceless glottal fricative, sometimes called a voiceless glottal transition or an aspirate, is a type of sound used in some spoken languages. It is familiar to English-speakers as the \"h\" sound in \"hut\". The symbol in the International Phonetic Alphabet that represents this sound is ⟨h⟩."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/IPA_Unicode_0x0068.svg/330px-IPA_Unicode_0x0068.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Voiceless_glottal_fricative","wikidata":"Q373478"},{"title":"Aspiration (album)","blocks":[{"text":"Aspiration is a compilation album by American composer Bill Laswell, released on March 15, 2011, by Metastation."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/7d/Bill_Laswell_-_Aspiration.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aspiration_(album)","wikidata":"Q18354722"}],"images":[],"sounds":{"aspiration":[{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/8e/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-aspiration.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/8/8e/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-aspiration.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-aspiration.wav.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/8/8e/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-aspiration.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-aspiration.wav.ogg"},{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/ab/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-JutishMale-aspiration.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/a/ab/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-JutishMale-aspiration.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-JutishMale-aspiration.wav.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/a/ab/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-JutishMale-aspiration.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-JutishMale-aspiration.wav.ogg"}]},"pictures":[{"title":"Grey Carpet from above","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/Grey_Carpet_from_above.jpg/500px-Grey_Carpet_from_above.jpg","ratio":1.3333333333333333,"link":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Grey_Carpet_from_above.jpg","share":0.318125},{"title":"Eastern grey kangaroo (Macropus giganteus) Mount Annan composite of 6","image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Eastern_grey_kangaroo_%28Macropus_giganteus%29_Mount_Annan_